    ],
    "Instructions": {
        "Text": "Ladies and gentlemen of the jury, you are instructed as follows:\n\nThe plaintiffs, the State of Alabama and Mobile River Communities, allege that ExxonTexaco Corporation created a public nuisance and caused harm through negligent pollution. The State must prove by a preponderance of the evidence that:\n\n1. ExxonTexaco controlled or contributed to the contamination of the public waterway or adjacent land.\n2. The defendant's conduct was unreasonable in light of the known or reasonably discoverable risks.\n3. The defendant's actions caused actual harm or interference with public rights.\n\nA public nuisance is an unreasonable interference with a right common to the general public. The evidence may include internal communications, scientific data, regulatory reports, and testimony from experts and residents.\n\nIf you find the plaintiffs have proven each element by a preponderance of the evidence, you should find in their favor. If not, you must find for the defendant.\n\nYou are the sole judges of the credibility of witnesses and the weight to be given to the evidence. Your verdict must be based solely on the evidence presented and the law as I give it to you.",
        "Standard": "PreponderanceOfEvidence"
    },
